exports[`buncargo CLI output ci --help 1`] = `
"exit 0
--- stdout

Usage: buncargo ci [options] [-- <args>]

Start services in CI, prepare them, run a command, tear down

Options:
  --migrate                      Run migrations (and Prisma generate) after services start
  --seed                         Run migrations, then the seed command
  --schema=<migrate|push>        How the Prisma schema is applied: its migrations, or \`prisma db push\` (implies --migrate)
  --slot                         Hold one of the machine's check slots from before the services start until teardown
  --services=<names>             Start only these services (default: every configured one)
  --runtime=<docker|apple|auto>  Container runtime backend (default: docker)
  --help, -h                     Show this help message
  --                             Command to run with the checkout environment

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  preparation failed, or bad arguments; otherwise the command's own code

Examples:
  buncargo ci --migrate -- bun test             Services up, migrations applied, tests, teardown
  buncargo ci --seed                            Check that migrations and the seed apply cleanly
  buncargo ci --schema=push --slot -- bun test  A unit shard: the schema pushed, not migrated, inside a check slot


--- stderr
"
`;

